## Our changes relative to upstream

### 1. `mcp/` — an MCP server (our own code, not upstream)

`mcp/server.ts` (752 lines, 10 tools) is **entirely our addition**. It is **not**
upstream code; no upstream license obligation attaches to it beyond this project's own.

Why it exists (the file's own header explains this): the `bh` CLI is **interactive** —
every command that touches a mod asks the human to pick one from an `@inquirer/search`
prompt — and the bundled `dist/bannerlord-helper.js` also trips over a tsup treeshaking
bug (`assignWith is not defined`) in `info` / `search`.

The server therefore **does not shell out to the CLI for mod-scoped work**. Instead it
**reuses upstream's own library layer** (`src/helper`, `src/core`, `src/api`) and supplies
the module selection as a normal tool argument, so every tool is non-interactive.

| # | Tool |
|---|---|
| 1 | `bh_list_languages` |
| 2 | `bh_resolve_language` |
| 3 | `bh_list_local_modules` |
| 4 | `bh_search_nexusmods` |
| 5 | `bh_module_details` |
| 6 | `bh_generate_template` |
| 7 | `bh_translate_module` |
| 8 | `bh_create_external_translation` |
| 9 | `bh_identifier` |
| 10 | `bh_run_cli` |

> `bh_run_cli` is the only tool that spawns the bundled CLI (upstream's own
> `dist/bannerlord-helper.js`).

### 2. `src/api/nexusmod.ts` — rewritten to the Nexus GraphQL v2 API

Large rewrite (+287 / −153 lines, 434 changed). Now talks to the **official Nexus Mods
GraphQL API** (<https://api.nexusmods.com/v2/graphql>) instead of the previous approach:

- added constants for the game domain / id (`mountandblade2bannerlord`, `3174`) and the API key URL;
- added `MOD_FIELDS` / `SEARCH_DOCUMENT` / `DETAIL_DOCUMENT` GraphQL documents;
- added BBCode→text and HTML-entity decoding for mod descriptions,
  plus a `truncate()` helper;
- the API key is still read **only from the environment**
  (`NEXUS_API_KEY`, falling back to `NEXUSMODS_API_KEY`) — **no credential is hard-coded**.

### 3. `package.json`

- added `overrides: { "lodash.template": "4.5.0" }` and pinned that dependency exactly;
- added `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (used by our `mcp/` server).

## Credentials

This project **requires** a Nexus Mods personal API key for its Nexus tools.
The key is read from the environment only and is **never** stored in this repository.
Do not commit a file containing the key value.

